cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PBCM underwriting simulation for embedded merchant cash advances"
abstract: >-
  Fully synthetic, policy-consistent evaluation suite for the Platform
  Behavioral Credit Model (PBCM) described in "Underwriting embedded merchant
  cash advances from marketplace settlement data: a design blueprint with a
  policy-consistent synthetic evaluation" (manuscript version 3). Generates
  seller populations and repayment paths from a stated data-generating process,
  compares behavioural-feature underwriting with a bureau-proxy baseline on a
  held-out cohort with a frozen operating policy, estimates tier expected-loss
  prices under the offered terms, evaluates repayment monitoring rules against
  baselines, and reports descriptive approval parity. No platform, lender,
  customer or company data is used or required.
type: software
